he mattress was torn to shreds, the furniture was shattered, and the floor was lifted up\u2014clearly the person with the axe had continued to search in Dr. Aless's room. There was a small gilded clock in the room. Curiously, it too had escaped the hurricane-like destruction, falling from the table to the floor. The hands stopped at 12:24. [2015] Pecsin's eyes lit up. \"Our friend left a time schedule for his activities. This proves that he first attacked downstairs... Maxwell, does this clock keep good time?\" [2016] \"Yes, miss. All the clocks are accurate, although they're cheap. And I often wind them up to keep them all in sync.\" [2017] \"That's lucky,\" Raine murmured. \"The man is so stupid!\" [2018] \"What?\" Pauling exclaimed sharply. [2019] \"Oh, nothing, Mr. Pauling. I was just criticizing the stupidity of criminals in general.\" [2020] A baritone voice called up the stairs, \"Hey! Look what I found!\" [2021] They rushed down the stairs. A policeman stood in the hallway, holding a flashlight over a dark, dirty corner. Under the light, they saw three shards of glass, one of which was tied with a black long silk ribbon. [2022] Rene picked up the glass shard and brought it into the living room. He put the three shards together, and they formed a perfect circular piece of glass. [2023] \"A single lens,\" he said quietly. [2024] \"Oh my!\" Rowe whispered. [2025] \"A single lens?\" Maxwell blinked. \"Sir, that's quite strange. Dr. Al\u00e9s doesn't wear glasses. I've never seen one in the house, and I\u2014\"\n[2026] \"Dr. Sedra.\" Percy worriedly said. [2027] Chapter 23\n[2028] Symbolic Issue\n[2029] There was nothing to do at the scene. Maxwell accepted the advice and left the house, returning to his peaceful life in Tarrytown, leaving the energetic and hardworking Mr. Bowling to monitor the house, leaving two men to guard the alley and the back of the house - although you could not enter from the back, you would have to flatten the lush shrubs and the fallen